        "id": 162270,
        "name": "waedens",
        "username": "waedens",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/b3f665/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-16T14:04:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The potential market for a game can be inversely correlated to the amount of set up the game requires. SotM actually requires a relatively small setup. Tactical games require more, but are still not to bad. RPGs require a lot of setup. Not necessarily at the table, but leading up to the game. People working on characters and of course the GM has a ton of up front work to do. Is it worth it. I say yes, but I am a work hard, play hard kind of guy. Most people get done with their jobs and want to relax, not spend a bunch of time with pencil and paper working on making an adventure or updating their character.&nbsp;</p><p>Hopefully GtG will tap into another action adventure series with a similar play, power, draw deck based game that will bring us to new and interesting worlds (Space, Arabian nights, feudal Japan, etc.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:43:03.561Z",
