      {
        "id": 162273,
        "name": "dprcooke",
        "username": "dprcooke",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/{size}/1961_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-16T16:59:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"BlueHairedMeerkat\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/48/1967_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BlueHairedMeerkat:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>TheSoundOfTrees wrote:</b><br><blockquote>The problem, from a \"story\" point of view, is that, once the OblivAeon event happen, either the whole universe disappears, or alternate universes and timelines are no more accessible. And one of the prinicples of the game is that each fight we have is an \"alternate timeline\" one - not the fight in the story.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI'm pretty sure that's entirely unofficial, though. They've never said that's how it works, it's just what people like to think. So while I don't think they will (they've made way too big a deal of this being THE END for them to quietly launch more SotM stuff a few years down the line) there are no story reasons not to, beyond that it would be a new plot arc. The Void Guard variants attest to that, for a start.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Actually, I'm pretty certain that's almost  <em>exactly</em> &nbsp;what they've said. &nbsp;I'd have to dig through Christopher's forum posts, KS comments, and Q&amp;A transcriptions, but basically all the crossing of timelines and universes we've been seeing is OblivAeon's doing. &nbsp;Once OblivAeon happens, either he'll win and all universes will cease to be, or the heroes will win but the universes will effectively* cease to interact… they'll still exist, but they'll be separate from one another and no longer form a multiverse.</p>\n<p>*I say \"effectively\" since Christopher's exact words on the subject (in some other post) were something along the lines of \"travel between universes will be significantly more difficult\", which seems to indicate they might be leaving a [very, very] small door open for possible interraction between universes. &nbsp;But even if they are, said interraction would be significantly less frequent than we're seeing now.</p>\n<p>EDIT: I just realized you may have been referring to \"each fight is an alternate timeline\" when you said that that's entirely unofficial. &nbsp;If that's the case, I have no idea and you can ignore this post.</p>",
